# MyClaude logrotate configuration
# Install: sudo cp logrotate-myclaude /etc/logrotate.d/myclaude
#          (install.sh's install_logrotate() renders __REPO_DIR__ / __SERVICE_USER__ at install time)
#
# REWRITTEN 2026-10-27 after reading the live tree. The previous file had TWO stanzas
# and ZERO effective rotation:
#   * '__REPO_DIR__/logs/litellm.log' -- the live system writes its durable evidence to
#     '__REPO_DIR__/guard.log' at the repo ROOT (concurrency_guard's FileHandler).
#     litellm.log was archived to attic/ and logs/ is never written, so this stanza
#     matched nothing (missingok = silent no-op) while guard.log grew unbounded.
#   * '/var/log/nginx/myclaude*.log' -- the generated nginx site sets only
#     'access_log off' on /health and writes NO myclaude*.log; nginx's real logs are
#     /var/log/nginx/{access,error}.log, which the DISTRO's /etc/logrotate.d/nginx
#     already rotates, so a second stanza here would double-rotate.
# guard.log itself had NO stanza -- the one log that records every acquire/release/
# reclaim, the slow-OK asymmetry, and the 07:21:10 + 12:22:30 reclaims had no retention.
#
# copytruncate, NOT create+reload: concurrency_guard holds guard.log open via a
# logging.FileHandler (append mode). 'create' rotates the inode and leaves the handler
# writing to the renamed file; 'copytruncate' copies then truncates the SAME inode, so
# the open handler keeps appending with no reopen and no postrotate signal.
__REPO_DIR__/guard.log {
    daily
    rotate 14
    compress
    delaycompress
    missingok
    notifempty
    copytruncate
}
